    <ReasonableCauseExplanation documentId="ReasonableCause" softwareId="23017518" softwareVersionNum="2023v6.0">
      <ExplanationTxt>The organization was newly formed in February 2023, and the 2023 Form 990-EZ represents its first required filing with the Internal Revenue Service. As a new nonprofit, the organization was still establishing its administrative processes while focusing on launching programs and securing initial funding. The organization failed to timely file due to inexperience as a newly formed entity. Upon discovering this oversight, the organization immediately took steps to complete its filing. The organization has now implemented improved procedures to ensure all future filings will be completed on time, including engaging nonprofit counsel to prepare all annual returns and reports going forward. The organization takes its reporting responsibilities seriously and is committed to full compliance with all IRS requirements. Given that this is the first filing as a new organization and the good faith efforts to remedy the situation, the organization respectfully requests that the late filing penalties be abated.</ExplanationTxt>
    </ReasonableCauseExplanation>
